import{_ as t,c as o,o as r,ah as n}from"./chunks/framework.PvdZnrZd.js";const g=JSON.parse('{"title":"Squarespace connector","description":"Squarespace connector","frontmatter":{"title":"Squarespace connector","description":"Squarespace connector","author":"Chirag Tyagi"},"headers":[],"relativePath":"zenith/featured-app/connector/squarespace-connector.md","filePath":"zenith/featured-app/connector/squarespace-connector.md"}'),a={name:"zenith/featured-app/connector/squarespace-connector.md"};function s(p,e,l,c,i,h){return r(),o("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<p>The <strong><a href="/zenith/introduction/">Multi-vendor Marketplace</a></strong> app for Shopify has come up with yet another connector add-on namely <strong>Squarespace Connector</strong>.</p><p>The sellers who sell products on <a href="https://www.squarespace.com/ecommerce-website" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Squarespace</a> can effortlessly import their products into the Multi-vendor seller panel.</p><p>Thus, gets the simplest way to sell Squarespace products on Shopify.</p><p>Accordingly, inventory will be managed at both ends once an order is created/updated for the seller’s product at Squarespace or at Shopify.</p><p>To enable the <strong>Connector</strong>, visit the “<strong>Feature App</strong>” section of the app and activate the feature app.</p><h2 id="how-to-enable" tabindex="-1">How to Enable? <a class="header-anchor" href="#how-to-enable" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;How to Enable?&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Go to the <strong>Feature App</strong> section and enable the <strong>Squarespace Connector</strong> feature app.</p><p><img src="https://cdnblog.webkul.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/screenshot-ravikant-sh.webkul.com-2021.10.06-14_32_55-1200x590.png" alt="Squarespace Connector feature app"></p><p>Then, approve the additional charge of $25 USD/month over and above your current Multi-vendor app plan.</p><h2 id="admin-panel-configuration" tabindex="-1">Admin Panel Configuration <a class="header-anchor" href="#admin-panel-configuration" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Admin Panel Configuration&quot;">​</a></h2><p>To configure the settings, visit the admin panel <strong>Configurations</strong>&gt;&gt;<strong>Connector Configuration</strong>&gt;&gt;select the connector.</p><p><img src="https://cdnblog.webkul.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/screenshot-ravikant-sh.webkul.com-2021.10.06-14_36_32-1200x590.png" alt="Squarespace Connector- admin"></p><p>From this section, you can configure the settings:-</p><p><img src="https://cdnblog.webkul.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/screenshot-ravikant-sh.webkul.com-2021.10.06-14_39_12-1-1200x854.png" alt="Squarespace Connector"></p><p><img src="https://cdnblog.webkul.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/squarespace-1200x580.webp" alt="edit"></p><p><strong>Note:-</strong> Once the order is created at the admin Shopify store for the connector product then the same order will be created on seller&#39;s squarespace store also.</p><p>Even, the admin will get a reference order number like below that will be shown order section of the seller&#39;s Squarespace store.</p><p><img src="https://cdnblog.webkul.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2023/02/screenshot_from_2022_12_27_12_51_33-3-1200x595.png" alt="screenshot_from_2022_12_27_12_51_33-3"></p><p>That&#39;s all about the admin end configurations. Let&#39;s move on to the seller panel configuration.</p><h2 id="seller-panel-configuration" tabindex="-1">Seller Panel Configuration <a class="header-anchor" href="#seller-panel-configuration" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Seller Panel Configuration&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Now, the seller needs to manage the configuration from the Multi-vendor seller panel. Visit the seller panel <strong>Configuration</strong>&gt;&gt;<strong>Squarespace Configuration</strong>.</p><p><img src="https://cdnblog.webkul.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/screenshot-ravikant-sh.webkul.com-2021.10.07-15_39_37-1200x590.png" alt="screenshot-ravikant-sh.webkul.com-2021.10.07-15_39_37"></p><p><img src="https://cdnblog.webkul.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/screenshot-ravikant-sh.webkul.com-2021.10.06-15_35_42-1200x732.png" alt="Squarespace Connector seller"></p><p>Here, the seller needs to configure the Squarespace details such as unit weight, store currency, Squarespace API key. Let&#39;s see how the seller will get the API keys.</p><h2 id="how-to-get-api-keys" tabindex="-1">How to Get API Keys? <a class="header-anchor" href="#how-to-get-api-keys" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;How to Get API Keys?&quot;">​</a></h2><p>To get the keys, log in to the Squarespace portal and visit the Home:</p><p><img src="https://cdnblog.webkul.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/Screenshot-2021-10-06T164101.501-1200x588.png" alt="Squarespace Connector"></p><p>Now, go to <strong>Settings</strong>:</p><p><img src="https://cdnblog.webkul.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/screenshot-vuvuzela-finch-lmjg.squarespace.com-2021.10.06-16_39_35-1200x590.png" alt="Squarespace Connector settings"></p><p>Go to Advanced Settings:</p><p><img src="https://cdnblog.webkul.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/Screenshot-2021-10-06T164350.344-1200x592.png" alt="Squarespace Connector settings"></p><p>Now, click Developer API Key:</p><p><img src="https://cdnblog.webkul.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/Screenshot-2021-10-06T164642.616-1200x600.png" alt="Squarespace Connector keys"></p><p>There, you will get the option to generate keys. You need to enter the key name and enable the required permissions.</p><p><img src="https://cdnblog.webkul.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/Screenshot-2021-10-06T164747.248-1200x587.png" alt="Squarespace Connector permissions"></p><p>Required Permissions will be:-</p><ul><li><strong>Forms</strong> - Read Only</li><li><strong>Products</strong> - Read and Write</li><li><strong>Inventory</strong> - Read and Write</li><li><strong>Orders</strong> - Read and Write</li><li><strong>Transactions</strong> - Read Only</li><li><strong>Profile</strong> - read Only</li></ul><p><img src="https://cdnblog.webkul.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/Screenshot-2021-10-06T164952.475-1200x587.png" alt="Squarespace Connector"></p><p><img src="https://cdnblog.webkul.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/Screenshot-2021-10-06T165329.425-1200x589.png" alt="Squarespace Connector"></p><p>Hit the <strong>Generate</strong> button and you will have the keys.</p><p><img src="https://cdnblog.webkul.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/screenshot-vuvuzela-finch-lmjg.squarespace.com-2021.10.06-16_59_09-1-1200x590.png" alt="API Key "></p><p>Once done, the sellers can proceed to import products from Squarespace to the Multi-vendor app.</p><h2 id="tag-mapping" tabindex="-1">Tag Mapping <a class="header-anchor" href="#tag-mapping" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Tag Mapping&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Before the product import, the seller needs to map the admin’s store product tags with the tags of his/her Squarespace store.</p><p><strong>Note</strong>:- Make sure that the admin has enabled the “<strong>Restrict Tag</strong>” tab from the multi-vendor admin panel.</p><p>For this, the seller will visit the <strong>Tag Mapping</strong> section and then, select the admin’s collection to map with his/her own Squarespace store’s collection.</p><p><img src="https://cdnblog.webkul.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/Screenshot-2021-10-07T160655.950-1200x591.png" alt="Screenshot-2021-10-07T160655.950"></p><h2 id="seller-importing-products-–-squarespace-to-shopify" tabindex="-1">Seller Importing Products – Squarespace to Shopify <a class="header-anchor" href="#seller-importing-products-–-squarespace-to-shopify" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Seller Importing Products – Squarespace to Shopify&quot;">​</a></h2><p>After all these settings, the seller will proceed to import products from his/her Squarespace store to the admin’s Shopify store.</p><p>Clicking the <strong>Import Product</strong> button, the seller will have two methods to import products.</p><p><img src="https://cdnblog.webkul.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/screenshot-ravikant-sh.webkul.com-2021.10.07-16_10_58-1200x590.png" alt="screenshot-ravikant-sh.webkul.com-2021.10.07-16_10_58"></p><ul><li><strong>Method 1</strong>: The seller will <strong>select the duration</strong> to import products from Squarespace to Shopify.</li><li><strong>Method 2:</strong> The seller will enter the <strong>comma-separated product IDs</strong> (that the seller wants to import)..</li></ul><p><img src="https://cdnblog.webkul.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/screenshot-ravikant-sh.webkul.com-2021.10.07-16_14_09-1200x794.png" alt="screenshot-ravikant-sh.webkul.com-2021.10.07-16_14_09"></p><p>This way, the products will get imported.</p><p>Please note: Sellers will have to update the products manually in case there is any updates on product on seller&#39;s square space store.</p><p><img src="https://cdnblog.webkul.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2023/01/squarespace-1200x509.png" alt="squarespace"></p><h2 id="squarespace-connector-price-rule" tabindex="-1">Squarespace Connector Price Rule <a class="header-anchor" href="#squarespace-connector-price-rule" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Squarespace Connector Price Rule&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Let the sellers create price rules to manage the product price of the seller’s Squarespace to the merchant’s store.</p><p><img src="https://cdnblog.webkul.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2019/11/Dashboard-Seller-%E2%80%A2-Multivendor-MarketPlace-2-1200x627.png" alt="connector price rule"></p><p>So, the sellers will have a new menu named <strong>Connector Price Rule</strong> in the configuration menu of the app.</p><p>From here, the seller can create price rules based on which the seller’s product price will be calculated on the merchant’s store.</p><p>Now, the seller needs to enable “Price Rule” status and select the options as increase/decrease price, the price will be changed by a fixed amount or a percentage amount,</p><p>enter the amount that needs to be changed.</p><p><img src="https://cdnblog.webkul.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/screenshot-ravikant-sh.webkul.com-2021.10.07-17_30_10-1200x805.png" alt="Squarespace Connector Price rule"></p><p>So, that&#39;s all about the Squarespace Connector feature app.</p><h3 id="demo-details" tabindex="-1">Demo <strong>Details</strong> <a class="header-anchor" href="#demo-details" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Demo **Details**&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Follow the below link to use the demo of the Multi-vendor Marketplace app: <a href="https://multivendor-marketplace-5.myshopify.com/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://multivendor-marketplace-5.myshopify.com/</a></p><p>Thanks for reading !!</p>',68)])])}const d=t(a,[["render",s]]);export{g as __pageData,d as default};
